  "note": "Stage 3 TypeScript's own repository pins, deliberately separate from docs/core-representative-corpus.json. That file's validate_manifest() (tools/core_representative_benchmark.py) hard-codes 'exactly six repositories', a rust/python-only language allowlist, a single-extension-per-language assumption, and requires every entry to carry nonempty semantic_cases before it will run at all -- all Rust/Python-specific, none of which this repository's TypeScript pins need or satisfy (empty semantic_cases; TypeScript needs both .ts and .tsx). Adding these three entries there directly broke that file's own already-gated test suite (2 failures) before this manifest was split out - reverted in 00ba4b1, not left broken. No Stage 3 site-selector tool reads semantic_cases at all (confirmed by grep before either version of this pin was written), so this manifest omits the field entirely rather than populating it with placeholder data.",
